  "notes": "Found on 2026-11-25 by a search over the cyclic group of order 259, written as Z_7 x Z_37. With s = 36, for which s^2 = 1 modulo 259 (s is 1 modulo 7 and -1 modulo 37), row A as submitted is unchanged by k -> -sk, row D is unchanged by k -> sk, and row C is row B carried by k -> sk: C(k) = B(sk). All four rows are unchanged by multiplication by 44, of order 9 modulo 259. The row sums are 31, 5, 5, 5. The search is an exact join over rows constant on the orbits of these maps, exhaustive for this s and this group of multipliers and for nothing else; the run record gives its patterns and counts. The Goethals-Seidel array of these rows is a Hadamard matrix of order 1036. The rows also give a symmetric Hadamard matrix of order 1036, by a variant of the propus array that was worked out for this board and has not been reviewed; the run record states it, and the verifier does not check that matrix. The run record lists what was read on 2026-11-25 about the status of the order: a census dated May 2025 lists v = 259 as undecided for symmetric Hadamard matrices of order 4v, and the search of the literature and public repositories found no symmetric Hadamard matrix of order 1036. This reports the search and does not claim priority, and the result has not been reviewed."
